WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.770
Your outboard is about to sit
through a whole Ontario winter.

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.170
How you leave it this fall
decides how spring goes.

3
00:00:08.658 --> 00:00:13.668
Start with water. Water left in
the motor freezes, and ice expands.

4
00:00:14.518 --> 00:00:16.408
That's why storage position matters.

5
00:00:17.018 --> 00:00:19.108
The motor has to sit so it drains.

6
00:00:20.856 --> 00:00:25.706
Check the gear oil. If it comes
out milky, water is getting in.

7
00:00:25.996 --> 00:00:28.306
Stop running it and get it looked at.

8
00:00:29.527 --> 00:00:33.837
Then fuel. Ethanol in
pump gas soaks up water.

9
00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:38.277
Over a long sit, it can separate
and sink to the bottom of the tank,

10
00:00:39.127 --> 00:00:41.277
right where the fuel is drawn from.

11
00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:45.524
And the battery. A flat
battery can freeze.

12
00:00:45.854 --> 00:00:49.124
Charge it, disconnect it,
and keep it topped up.

13
00:00:50.265 --> 00:00:52.635
The catch? There's no one recipe.

14
00:00:53.545 --> 00:00:58.385
Fogging, flushing and storage steps change
by engine, so follow the manual for your

15
00:00:58.405 --> 00:01:02.475
serial number. And never run
it without cooling water.

16
00:01:03.743 --> 00:01:09.743
Want it done right? Fill out the
service request at hbwservice.ca,

17
00:01:09.763 --> 00:01:12.853
then drop off your boat
by trailer or by water.

18
00:01:13.543 --> 00:01:14.653
We take it from there.

19
00:01:15.263 --> 00:01:18.013
We're closed December
first to April first.
